// spec: an explicit type converts to nothing and nothing converts to it without a cast (design.md 33): not a number (a literal either), not another explicit type of the same underlying type, not an explicit bool to bool outside a condition; it has arithmetic and comparisons with its own type only, and an explicit bool has no arithmetic
